  "limits": [
    "Effect limited to the named work. Keep outside work, launch gaps, engine contention, request admission/acceptance, clocks and external dependencies fixed. Changed resource interference, joint producers and earlier tokens altering later execution have their own scope.",
    "The all-rank graph screen bounds removal of recorded target tasks of that label, including any observer contribution; no graph/eager/draft/host extrapolation. A high amount may contain waiting or compulsory work. Labels need not be distinct semantic candidates.",
    "Per-layer graph bounds for FFN norm/hash/Pre assume one local occurrence per layer lies on a serial TP critical path, and fully serialize DP groups. HcPre uses the largest time over both attention and FFN. The eager hash-only budget generously includes the full score+selection stage; results assume the archived EP retirement and earliest release model. No claim about physical bounds under a different schedule.",
    "Uniform per-step thresholds assume one exposed saving on each six-token scheduling step of each affected request and no propagation to requests outside that step. Chunk count and worker steps are different; no inferred token-by-token correspondence. Pure local changes can still propagate across DPs via EP if dependencies are changed.",
    "The 1% guide is per metric. The unprofiled control triplets are empirical sensitivity under a uniform hypothetical shift; strict separation requires exceeding its boundary. They neither set a future minimum detectable gain nor invalidate a smaller real improvement."
  ],
